<folder_context path="adapters">
<reusable_module_context name="platform adapters">
Each registered adapter detects a consumer platform and concrete variant, performs a read-only
capability check for the concrete export, Pulls one exact component commit into usable
project-local state, Removes its root declaration and manager-owned materialization, and Inspects
local state. Pull is the adapter operation; declaration editing is only its private first step.
The lifecycle service persists the initially selected adapter/variant and verifies it before
later pulls.
</reusable_module_context>
<system_invariant name="one commit">
Every binding of one dependency uses LockedDependency.Commit. Floating pins and independent
ecosystem resolution are forbidden.
</system_invariant>
<system_invariant name="preserve variants">
Detection chooses a variant only during initial add. Pull uses the stored variant or fails with
an actionable mismatch/missing-tool error; it never silently redetects another manager.
</system_invariant>
<system_invariant name="real materialization">
A successful Pull means the platform can resolve or import the dependency without a second
manual package-manager command. It repairs missing project-local materialization even when the
manifest entry and resolved commit are unchanged. Remove invokes native manager semantics so
root lock entries and local installations converge while unrelated and transitively required
dependencies remain.
</system_invariant>
<settled_decision name="unsupported fallback">
Capability returns the typed NotWirable error only for a source shape the concrete variant
cannot represent. Initial selection may replace that binding with one submodule fallback.
Missing tools, network/auth failures, and saved bindings never trigger fallback.
</settled_decision>
<settled_decision name="build composition">
CMake, Gradle, MSBuild, Maven, and Meson consume the checkout owned by the submodule binding.
They do not clone, copy, or own a second checkout.
</settled_decision>
<verification_and_unit_test_criteria>
Cover capability/pull/remove/inspect, exact commit pins, missing-materialization repair,
idempotence, saved variants, malformed native files, missing tools, rollback-owned files, and no
deletion of unrelated or transitively required entries. Native evidence runs through the public
CLI and proves the dependency can be used.
</verification_and_unit_test_criteria>
</folder_context>
